  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of ZrZnSe₃ crystallizes in the orthorhombic space group Amm2 (No. 38), with a unit cell containing 20 atoms—Zr₄Zn₄Se₁₂—distributed over six independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis shows Zr centers coordinated by six Se neighbors in an octahedral motif, while Zn adopts a tetrahedral Se coordination environment. Se centers display several environments, including a trigonal bipyramidal motif and lower-coordinate Zn/Zr-containing environments. The geometric neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component spanning all 20 sites. Validated polyhedron-sharing relations reveal corner- and edge-sharing between trigonal bipyramidal Se polyhedra, corner-sharing between tetrahedral Zn and octahedral Zr polyhedra, and edge-sharing between Zn tetrahedra and Zr octahedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
